opam-version: "2.0"
synopsis: "The ABCI socket transport over any Mirage_flow, on Lwt"
description: """
Serves the native ABCI transport -- length-delimited protobuf over a stream,
which is what CometBFT uses by default -- through

  Socket_server.Make (Flow : Mirage_flow.S)

Functorised over Mirage_flow.S rather than opening sockets itself, so this one
package serves both Unix (via mirage-flow-unix, see cometbft-unix) and
MirageOS/Solo5 unikernels (via a Tcpip stack). It does not depend on unix, and
deliberately does not depend on h2 either: gRPC lives in cometbft-grpc so that
a socket-only unikernel stays small.

Lwt is not a preference here but a constraint: MirageOS has no Eio backend, so
a unikernel-capable server has to be Lwt-based.
"""
maintainer: ["gilbahat"]
authors: ["gilbahat"]
license: "ISC"
homepage: "https://github.com/reuna-labs/ocaml-cometbft"
bug-reports: "https://github.com/reuna-labs/ocaml-cometbft/issues"
dev-repo: "git+https://github.com/reuna-labs/ocaml-cometbft.git"
depends: [
  "ocaml" {>= "4.14"}
  "dune" {>= "3.0"}
  "cometbft" {= version}
  "lwt"
  "cstruct" {>= "6.0.0"}
  "mirage-flow" {>= "4.0.0"}
  "logs"
  "alcotest" {with-test}
  "alcotest-lwt" {with-test}
]
build: [["dune" "build" "-p" name "-j" jobs]]
